{"skill":{"slug":"pdf-tools","displayName":"PDF Tools"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1770373530803,"changelog":"Initial release of PDF Tools.\n\n- View, extract, and edit PDF files using Python scripts.\n- Supports text extraction (by page or all pages), text overlay, and limited text replacement.\n- Merge, split (by page or range), and rotate PDF pages.\n- Retrieve PDF metadata and structure in text or JSON formats.\n- All scripts work with standard Python libraries (pdfplumber, PyPDF2).\n- Includes workflow patterns for common PDF manipulation tasks.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":4121,"sha256":"f349ffff05319889e9e139d4102e6e92d026398700a9528f5e6eb10c650c8cfc","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2999,"sha256":"b75473a85bfca999134edb96dc12886a4e3a0c3ed044d1768ec9900c1e9a5715","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/libraries.md","size":3923,"sha256":"c03e8a570fc1f17a2879c8806b13c896128b38fd5ecb74649978a7d412874059","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/edit_text.py","size":5504,"sha256":"234c8406da9aeabbaa7c270e7fa70b67f924b9594cdf8146091678bda0e92f49","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/extract_text.py","size":1964,"sha256":"28844b75c2f520251fc4aa71c096c85ddf72e3772f6860de7c48fda2a66ae83c","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/merge_pdfs.py","size":1306,"sha256":"c9bf0e88bb8c7192d7d8a6fd4dae3359a72d08a442d0fff28ea68e4cb0ff2cdb","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/pdf_info.py","size":2062,"sha256":"fc6d453f80bcc4988b30347f181718a645a3098e3f90889f212de5c641389aa8","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/rotate_pdf.py","size":2352,"sha256":"784e15892bc0d1b50c8cae6300dfe9e87494ece28a6fa45b1e95cb61a8585ba8","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/split_pdf.py","size":3272,"sha256":"ff28b0e63ae5084680c595eb591ff93cd7fc81f0bfa5c86538c88cade74f43e3","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2241,"sha256":"c7f1d9ad6038fe7bbcc8db9aa9d4f68b77a2de9a40bb1c78a3f3e2a383bdef9d","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789036664889,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"3ed83a0fdba83d5f6ee073b8be81b7141307616d353133ead5364c1dda84e85b","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3ed83a0fdba83d5f6ee073b8be81b7141307616d353133ead5364c1dda84e85b","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: pdf-tools\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle for PDF tools is classified as benign. All Python scripts (`edit_text.py`, `extract_text.py`, `merge_pdfs.py`, `pdf_info.py`, `rotate_pdf.py`, `split_pdf.py`) perform standard PDF manipulation tasks using well-known libraries (pdfplumber, PyPDF2, reportlab). File operations are limited to reading specified input PDFs and writing output PDFs or text files to designated paths. There are no network calls, attempts to access sensitive system files or environment variables, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation. The `SKILL.md` and `README.md` files provide clear, benign instructions for using the PDF tools and do not contain any prompt injection attempts to subvert the agent's behavior or access unauthorized data.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161827697},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":52,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789036664889},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This PDF utility skill does what it says and shows no hidden data theft, persistence, or privilege escalation, though users should be careful with file outputs and unpinned Python dependencies.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill reads user-specified PDFs and writes user-specified output text/PDF files or output directories, which is proportionate for PDF manipulation; no credential access, network calls in runtime scripts, broad indexing, or unrelated local file traversal was found.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Installation uses ordinary pip commands for pdfplumber, PyPDF2, and reportlab, but dependency versions and hashes are not pinned, and SKILL.md omits reportlab even though edit_text.py imports it.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions use broad natural-language examples and say the agent will choose a script automatically, but the actual commands are task-specific and mutating operations require explicit input and output paths.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No background workers, scheduled tasks, memory writes, tool wrapping, privilege escalation, or cross-session persistence were found beyond normal skill installation in the OpenClaw skills directory.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is local PDF extraction, metadata inspection, merging, splitting, rotating, and text overlay/replacement; the bundled scripts implement those PDF-focused operations without unrelated behavior.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only in an environment where local PDF read/write access is acceptable. Use explicit output paths, avoid reusing the original PDF path as output unless you intend to overwrite it, keep backups for important documents, and prefer a virtual environment with pinned dependency versions for pdfplumber, PyPDF2, and reportlab.","findings":"[TP4] unexpected: Overridden: workspace inspection found separate scripts for extraction, metadata, merge, split, rotate, and edit operations, so the claimed description-behavior mismatch is not supported by the artifact.\n[SQP-2] expected: Partially accepted as user guidance: writing PDFs and extracted text is expected for this skill and output paths are shown, but the docs do not clearly warn about overwriting existing files or keeping backups.\n[SQP-1] expected: Downgraded: broad usage examples are normal skill invocation text; the artifact does not show unsafe background automation, and mutating scripts require explicit arguments.\n[LP3] expected: Downgraded: explicit permission scoping would be better, but the disclosed local read/write authority matches the PDF manipulation purpose and no excessive privilege behavior was found.\n[SQP-2] expected: Accepted as a low-risk documentation issue: SKILL.md documents output-producing commands but could be clearer that merge, split, rotate, edit, and text extraction with -o persist files to disk.\n[T08] expected: Accepted as a supply-chain note: dependencies are installed from PyPI without pinned versions or hashes, which is common but less reproducible and should be handled in an isolated environment.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789036664889}}}}}